.TH CTI-CHECKIN-CHECK 1 "2026-11-22" "cti-agent 1.7" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-checkin-check \- run-checkin's file checks around a heartbeat
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cti\-checkin\-check
.BI \-\-guard\-wired " SETTINGS"
.BI \-\-guard " PATH"
.br
.B cti\-checkin\-check \-\-steering
.IR FILE ...
.br
.B cti\-checkin\-check
.BI \-\-tripped " COUNTS"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cti\-checkin\-check
makes the three checks
.BR run\-checkin (1)
needs around a beat. It reads and reports, and changes nothing. It is not
an operator command. It replaced three python3 heredocs in the runner; the
rules are the same.
.SH OPTIONS
Exactly one of the three:
.TP
.BI \-\-guard\-wired " SETTINGS" " \-\-guard" " PATH"
Before a beat: the root-owned
.I SETTINGS
file must run
.I PATH
(checkin\-bash\-guard) as the Bash PreToolUse hook, with
.B disableAllHooks
present and false. A hook whose command does not exist fails open, so the
path must be this box's own. Exit 0 when it does, 1 when it does not or
the file cannot be read; run\-checkin then refuses the beat.
.TP
.BI \-\-steering " FILE" ...
Before a beat: Claude Code's own config files in the service account's
reach (its settings.json and .claude.json). One line per file that cannot
be read as a JSON object, and per risky key set at the top level or under
any
.B projects
entry: hooks, permissions, mcpServers, enabledMcpjsonServers,
enableAllProjectMcpServers, env, apiKeyHelper, awsAuthRefresh,
awsCredentialExport, otelHeadersHelper, statusLine, enabledPlugins,
extraKnownMarketplaces, allowedTools. A key set to null, false, 0, an empty
string, list or object sets nothing. A file that does not exist is skipped,
and one reached twice through a link is read once. Nothing printed means
clean; on Linux, any line refuses the beat.
.TP
.BI \-\-tripped " COUNTS"
After a beat: the limits checkin\-bash\-guard enforced, from its counter
file, as
.BR "limit reached for bash, alert" ;
nothing when it enforced none. Exit 1 when the file cannot be read or its
.B tripped
is not a list, which run\-checkin reports as an anomaly.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Checked (and for \-\-guard\-wired, wired).
.TP
.B 1
Not wired, or the counter file could not be read.
.TP
.B 2
Bad arguments: give exactly one of the three.
.SH EXAMPLES
What run\-checkin runs before a beat:
.PP
.EX
cti\-checkin\-check \-\-guard\-wired /opt/cti\-agent/checkin\-settings.json \e
  \-\-guard /opt/cti\-agent/bin/checkin\-bash\-guard
cti\-checkin\-check \-\-steering ~/.claude/settings.json ~/.claude.json
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/cti\-agent/bin/cti\-checkin\-check
The helper, root-owned. run\-checkin refuses a beat without it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR run\-checkin (1),
.BR checkin\-bash\-guard (1),
.BR cti\-checkin\-verdict (1)
